      "writtenOn": "2026-03-18T22:35:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, when I was logging rdcosts, I did see `rd_stats_y-\u003erdcost` can take the value of `INT64_MAX` at times.\n\nI think it\u0027s because `av1_txfm_search()` can output invalid rd stats (with an `rdcost` of `INT64_MAX`) because of the following check:\n\n```\n  // Account for minimum skip and non_skip rd.\n  // Eventually either one of them will be added to mode_rate\n  const int64_t min_header_rd_possible \u003d RDCOST(x-\u003erdmult, min_header_rate, 0);\n  if (min_header_rd_possible \u003e ref_best_rd) {\n    av1_invalid_rd_stats(rd_stats_y);\n    return 0;\n  }\n```\n\nI\u0027ll remove the `if` for `rd_stats`.",
      "parentUuid": "b4127be7_d05d4dc6",
      "revId": "d54b1a4b6978b515031707a72948e06bb0b76edb",
